    {
      "id": 185468,
      "name": "hstein3",
      "username": "hstein3",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/hstein3/{size}/2159_2.png",
      "created_at": "2016-11-27T02:54:05.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I haven’t.  Do you have the game log by any chance?   There is an off chance that after the shuffle and draw that the Assassin is still on top.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Ah, I play on a Nook, so I’m not sure I could access the log if I wanted to.</p>\n<p>But I know something was off here. I didnt hear the shuffle sound after searching the deck. And I rewound to replay the card several times and had the same result multiple times in a row; I’m assuming the shuffle shouldn’t have put the same card on top again and again.</p>\n<p>And yes, the rewinding made sure I could verify I was searching the deck.</p>\n<p>It might just be a one off, given that it disn’t repeat in the same match, but I wanted to see if there was something maybe I missed.</p>",
      "post_number": 6,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:10:59.293Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
