    {
      "id": 185469,
      "name": "jorgenp",
      "username": "jorgenp",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/j/958977/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2016-11-27T07:02:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Shuffles will always shuffle the same way if done at the same time.&nbsp; Rewinding resets the RNG seed to ensure the same shuffle comes out.&nbsp; That way, you can't cheat by repeatably rewinding until you get a good shuffle.</p><p>Now, if you were taking out a different instrument each time, that would cause different shuffles.&nbsp; If it was the same one, you will always get the same shuffle, though.</p>",
      "post_number": 7,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:10:59.355Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
